    "body": "Gemini notes with reformatting and adding some links:\n\nJake Archibald introduced a pull request to add an abort callback mechanism to `AbortSignal` for better memory management, prompting discussion with Anne van Kesteren and Nicolò Ribaudo about implementation and TC39's role, with Keith Cirkel and Olli Pettay raising caution about potential open protocols.\nhttp://github.com/whatwg/dom/pull/1425\n\nPhilip Jägenstedt presented the \"stream HTML unsafe\" proposal, which is ready for Stage 2, leading to a detailed discussion with Simon Pieters, Jake Archibald, Noam Rosenthal, and Anne van Kesteren about script execution, deferred scripts, microtask handling, and the need to separate parser settings from document concepts.\nhttps://github.com/whatwg/html/issues/2142\n\nThe group also discussed the complexity of handling errors and node insertion, particularly the `prepend` operation for Declarative Shadow DOM, with Noam Rosenthal suggesting to defer `prepend` and Anne van Kesteren requesting a detailed write-up on the various streaming operations.\nhttps://github.com/whatwg/html/issues/11542",
